{%- set card = 'own' -%}
{%- set title = 'own, the per authority ridge backend' -%}
{% set intended %}
The own backend forecasts hourly demand for each of the {{ v('hierarchy.authorities') }} balancing
authorities in the backtest, 1 to {{ v('policy.horizons') }} hours after a daily origin at
{{ v('policy.issue_hour_utc') }}:00 UTC, with quantiles at {{ v('policy.quantile_levels') }}. It is one
of the two candidates the registry judges and the fallback the API serves when no candidate clears
every gate. It is meant for the demonstration of a day ahead process on EIA-930 data and for the
detector's residuals. It is not meant for grid operations, for any authority it was not fit on, for
horizons past two days, or for a live desk that has a weather forecast rather than the weather that
happened.
{% endset %}
{% set data %}
EIA-930 hourly demand from {{ v('data.eia.first_hour') }} to {{ v('data.eia.last_hour') }} for the
{{ v('data.eia.backtest_authorities') }} authorities with at least {{ v('data.eia.minimum_window_coverage') }}
clean coverage in both the validation and the test year, quarantined by named rules
({{ v('data.eia.quarantined_share') }} of rows), with Open-Meteo hourly temperature and humidity at
one stated location per authority (observed weather, stated on every figure). Training from
{{ v('data.windows.training_start') }}, validation from {{ v('data.windows.validation_start') }}, test
{{ v('data.windows.test_start') }} to {{ v('data.windows.test_end') }}.
{% endset %}
{% set fit %}
Per authority, a ridge regression of the ratio of demand to the scale (the mean of the week ending
at the origin) on Fourier terms (daily, weekly, yearly), day type and holiday dummies, lags at the
horizon's availability, heating and cooling degree hours against thresholds chosen on the validation
year from {{ v('backtest.own.threshold_candidates') }} candidate pairs, and their change against the
same hour lag, with the ridge penalty chosen on validation from {{ v('policy.ridge_penalties') }}
({{ v('backtest.own.search_fits') }} static fits in the search); then an expanding fit over every
origin through an incremental Gram matrix ({{ v('backtest.own.fits') }} solves over
{{ v('backtest.own.origins') }} origins in {{ v('backtest.own.fit_seconds') }} seconds of fitting and
{{ v('backtest.own.predict_seconds') }} of prediction). Quantiles by relative conformal residual
quantiles per {{ v('policy.conformal_horizon_bucket_hours') }} hour horizon bucket, calibrated on the
validation year. Chosen on validation: {{ v('backtest.own.chosen_on_validation') }}. Version
`{{ v('registry.own.version') }}`.
{% endset %}
